coupons can be an effective way to grow  your business but you've got to make  sure that you're making money from it  and you're testing them hi I'm Evan  Carmichael your friend in all things  entrepreneurship and today i'm answering  a question from one of our readers james  who wanted to know if he should use  couponing for his business and what the  pros and cons were so thanks to the  question James I know as entrepreneurs  we're always looking for different ways  to grow our businesses and experimenting  with different things with any marketing  in general that you're doing for your  company you want to test it make sure  it's delivering results on a small scale  before you expand a big mistake a lot of  times that we make is we get so excited  about a new marketing idea that we put a  lot of dollars into it and it doesn't  work and we end up out a lot of money so  you want to make sure whatever you're  trying do a little small-scale test it  see if it's working if it is you keep  doing it spend more money on it expand  the program it was not kill it try  something else for coupons so there are  a couple ways to do it usually it's  either one to bring in new business so  you have a discount I don't know what  you're selling but a discount on your  product or service a way you can use it  as a partner with other businesses so a  friend of mine runs a little gym  franchise where they help kids come in  and teach them gymnastics and he'll  partner up with local businesses around  him and allow them to give a coupon to  their customers for discount at the  class the idea with this is you get a  coupon for your first class so you can  come in either get the first class for  free or get the first class I've  discounted rate and then hopefully  they'll love it and they'll sign up for  the program and he'll have them in there  for year after year to year of the year  so you may be losing money on that first  class but you're gaining new customers  so it's one way to do it the second way  is to encourage  assisting customers to buy more or try  new product or services you might be  offering so example the salsa school  that I'm involved in will often as a new  introductory workshop so if they're  usually they're selling salsa classes  but they might have a new type of dance  that they want to introduce it could be  West Coast Swing or could be kazoomba  could be cha-cha whatever it is they  might put on a special deal if you sign  up for this salsa class you can also get  this kizomba class their West Coast  Swing class at a discounted rate and  it's to encourage people to try it to  see people are interested in if they  like the class if they like the  instructor and if they do it all works  out then they'll come back for more and  they'll keep coming back and keep coming  back and so even though you lose a  little bit of money on that first class  again the idea is that they keep coming  back over and over and over again you  want them to try whatever your product  or service is so those are the two most  common methods one get new people in and  to get current people to try out  whatever new product or service that you  have the danger here is that you spend a  lot of time and money fulfilling these  coupons and they're not going to  continue buying from you and this is the  biggest fear that a lot of people have  had with couponing sites like Groupon  where they get bombarded with business  new customers come in but they only by  that deal and they never come back and a  lot of groupons that people have have  purchased that's exactly what happened  you know the businesses get slammed all  these customers come in at the same time  over a short period of time they're just  buying that deal which is at a steep  discount and then they never come back  again to that business and so that's a  loss right if you're losing money on  your first transaction and then the  customer never comes back to you again  that's a big loss to you hopefully made  a good first impression with them maybe  they'll refer somebody on to you but  that's not the type of kind that you  want to attract so you want to make sure  that in your marketing you're going  after the right people ideal potential  clients for you and that the deal makes  sense that you're giving up something  you know there's some value there but  you're not losing your shirt over it and  you have to start tracking in  drinkin versions are these people coming  back to your business and buying more  and more and more from you if they're  not look at the offering look at the  look at who you're targeting and maybe  it makes sense to revamp it a little bit  see if there's another way to make it  work or maybe the coupon in strategy is  just not a right fit for your business  and you only can figure that out through  testing so maybe a lot of information on  couponing but those are my opinions on  the pros and the cons I hope you'll  you'll test it out and see if it works  for you for those of you watching if you  liked the video please give it a thumbs  up below I love to see those come in and  I'd love to hear you have to think if  you want leave a comment under this  video I always read those and I usually  respond so thank you and I'll see you on  the next episode  you
 

